  "stage": "synthesis-review",
  "summary": "The concise First Sunday of Advent study independently explains why the disciples can welcome their Judge and how communicants can await the birth of the Son they have received, readings I recovered before consulting the expansive study and verified against Gregory I.1.3\u20135, Chrysostom\u2019s Homily 24, Aquinas on Romans 13, lectio 3, Augustine on Psalm 85 \u00a7\u00a76 and 10\u201312, Bellarmine on Psalm 84, exposition 12, and Gu\u00e9ranger p. 137. I inspected all ten pages of the passing working proof (SHA-256 30dc1bcc6565f880f938a4b6048bb29795f2d4c05ce68b2ae321de6d5c1ea237), finding all eleven appointments and four senses on page 1, Jesus teaching in Jerusalem at Luke 21:25\u201333 with the event date unresolved and the two proposed composition dates separately identified on page 2, substantive themes on pages 3\u20134, and developed comparisons beginning on page 5."
